WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:07.760
Satoru Gojo, without any doubt, is one of&nbsp;
the coolest anime characters every created.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.760
And yet, what makes his character so intriguing&nbsp;
is not his unimaginable power or his fantastic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:19.680
sense of humor, but the tragic irony that&nbsp;
lies beneath them. Who then is Satoru Gojo?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.880
What does it mean to be the strongest?&nbsp;
What is actually going on behind those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.840
cold and clear eyes? And why does he&nbsp;
cover them? It's time to find out.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.720
Gojo is one of the most influential characters in&nbsp;
JuJutsu Kaisen. And I mean, being the strongest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.747
curse user out there, how could he not be.&nbsp;
The biggest strength Akutami has as an author,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.747 --> 00:00:54.000
is that he takes a lot of inspiration from other&nbsp;
Shounen stories, combines and expands upon them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.440
and ultimately makes them even more intriguing&nbsp;
and fascinating as they already were. Satoru Gojo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:06.240
is no exception. Many traits of his can quite&nbsp;
easily be traced back to other characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:12.320
but in the end he emerges as one of the most&nbsp;
unique and complex personalities out there.

00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:23.840
If you had to pick one word to describe&nbsp;
Satoru Gojo, I believe there is no doubt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.640
that 'Strength' is the only fit.&nbsp;
Gojo is the pinnacle of the JuJutsu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:33.200
world. If you need any proof, he is to&nbsp;
curses what Sukuna is to the Sorcerers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:40.400
An unbeatable force of nature that can only&nbsp;
be sealed and not actually killed. To fully&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:46.640
understand the tragedy of his character, you have&nbsp;
to understand what strength means for Gojo and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.440
how it dominates every aspect of his&nbsp;
life as well as his role in the story.

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:56.160
Being the strongest character in the story, he&nbsp;
serves as a sign-post to both the audience and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.160 --> 00:02:03.280
protagonists, what is actually possible in this&nbsp;
world, and how far behind they actually still are.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.800
Gojo's fighting style and the respect and fear&nbsp;
he enjoys from both friends and foes alike&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:14.800
is something we know from many other stories.&nbsp;
Netero in Hunter x Hunter,Shanks in One Piece,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:18.400
Shanks in Fairy Tail or All Might in Boku no Hero.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:22.800
Like all of them, Gojo has a very&nbsp;
easy-going, boyish sort of personality,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:28.160
that is immediately replaced by pure strength&nbsp;
and authority when his patience is tested.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:39.200
He is the the sort of character that almost&nbsp;
single-handedly holds the balance in the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.520
and the moment they are removed, chaos&nbsp;
erupts. While personality and look wise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:47.440
Gojo could be considered a cooler and&nbsp;
more entertaining version of Kakashi,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:53.600
as a teacher, he comes closer to All Might, in&nbsp;
that he is not exactly the best at teaching, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.400 --> 00:03:00.000
good and thoughtful enough to grow the&nbsp;
next generation of the "good guys". In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:06.480
fact Gojo has quite a bunch of wonderful, if&nbsp;
admittedly unconventional teaching moments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:18.320
And while they typical mentor-types usually&nbsp;
feel like their best days are already over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.880 --> 00:03:23.440
Gojo very much seems to be in his absolute&nbsp;
prime when we meet him in the story.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:26.640
Akutami makes it very clear very early on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.640 --> 00:03:32.480
what Gojo is capable of. Building on sharp&nbsp;
reflexes and a bright tactical intellect,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:37.280
his ridiculous amount of cursed energy and&nbsp;
physical strength as well as his capability&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:43.040
to perform a complete domain expansion are only&nbsp;
the tip of the ice berg. Gojo has been blessed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:49.840
not only with one, but TWO inherited abilities,&nbsp;
that in combination make him more god than man.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:04.400
The first of these is 'limitless', an ability that&nbsp;
allows Gojo to freely manipulate space and matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:09.360
down to an atomic level. This allows him&nbsp;
to slow down movement and decide what can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:15.280
or cannot touch him. We se this explained in&nbsp;
his fight with Jogo in the most hilarious way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:26.720
However Gojo is also able to&nbsp;
attract and repulse matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.680
giving him gravity and anti-gravity attributes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:35.760
alike. Finally, one of his most destructive&nbsp;
skills is combining both of these attributes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:41.360
which results in the complete annihilation&nbsp;
of any matter caught within the attack.

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.000
As if this wasn't scary enough however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:49.760
Gojo also has inherited the Six Eyes, an&nbsp;
ability that we still know very little about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.280
We know however, that it allows him&nbsp;
to perceive the world around him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:59.200
in terms of mass, cursed energy and so on and so&nbsp;
forth, making it the perfect fit for Limitless. 
 &nbsp;

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:21.360
The workings of these abilities are&nbsp;
actually incredibly cleverly crafted, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.360 --> 00:05:26.560
not related to the point of this video. Let me&nbsp;
know if you would like to learn more about that.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:33.680
The main takeaway point here, is that Gojo has had&nbsp;
the one thing values most in the world of JuJutsu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:40.240
raw, unmatched power that allows him to shape&nbsp;
the world around him in whatever way he pleases.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:51.840
And this is what brings us into the deeply nested&nbsp;
and layered realm of Satoru Gojo's personality.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:59.600
Due to his innate strength and claim to authority,&nbsp;
Gojo understandably is extremely confident in his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.600 --> 00:06:05.120
abilities, to the point where he believes himself&nbsp;
to be invincible. In relation to the central moral&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:10.720
argument of JuJutsu Kaisen - what constitutes&nbsp;
a good life - his view is quite different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:17.040
from Itadori's. While Itadori thinks that a good&nbsp;
life means enabling others to have a good death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:24.080
for Gojo, the answer is strength. In essence: When&nbsp;
you have strength you have agency over the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:30.960
your own life and that of others. Thus, while Yuji&nbsp;
expresses his believe in his hero complex, trying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:37.600
to save anyone waker than him and caring way to&nbsp;
much about others, Gojo is very self-centered and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:43.840
as we will see, has difficulties understanding&nbsp;
and caring for people weaker than him. He even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:49.400
tells Megumi to become stronger himself&nbsp;
and less reliant on others. (Greedy)

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:03.360
And yet, despite their polar&nbsp;
views on life, surprisingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:08.880
in the end Gojo and Itadori have one of the best&nbsp;
relationships in the show. On the surface, this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:13.560
seems to be due to their similarly extroverted&nbsp;
and genuinely funny personalities. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:14.880
truth is, that both Yuuji and Gojo try to get&nbsp;
rid of their loneliness. However, but their god&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:19.440
and hero complex keep them from truly creating any&nbsp;
meaningful and mutual relationships with others,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:24.240
as they can't let themselves be vulnerable by&nbsp;
letting anyone come close enough to help them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.240 --> 00:07:30.560
in return. As Gojo formulates it: Yuji and he&nbsp;
always go for the home run. In that way, while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.560 --> 00:07:38.080
expressed in different ways, both Yuji and Gojo&nbsp;
share the same fundamental weakness: Loneliness.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:43.680
To understand Gojo's sense of Loneliness, we&nbsp;
have to understand that despite his sense of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:50.560
superiority, luckily for everyone around him,&nbsp;
he actually has a strong sense of morality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:55.840
Gojo cares about the well-being of humanity and&nbsp;
and even more so for the people close to him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.480 --> 00:08:01.120
The society of JuJutsu sorcerers in their&nbsp;
preside to fight the curses that threaten&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.120 --> 00:08:06.000
humanity and human life have ironically&nbsp;
enough morphed into an environment that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:12.560
incredibly de-humanizing in of itself. All&nbsp;
that matters are blood-lines, influence and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:19.200
yes, strength. Despite being blessed with the&nbsp;
most desired trait amongst the sorcerers, or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.200 --> 00:08:25.440
maybe exactly because of it, Gojo knows very&nbsp;
well how corrupted this society has become.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:31.760
His big desire and rive therefore is not to&nbsp;
eradicate all curses or something similar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:39.840
but is pointed inwards and aims at revolutionizing&nbsp;
the system of the JuJutsu world itself.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:50.720
A very intriguing desire for him to have,&nbsp;
because it can't be solved by strength alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:57.120
but requires the one thing Gojo isn't great&nbsp;
at: Human relationships and comrades with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:03.200
common ideology. Gojou knows this. He doesn’t&nbsp;
want to be the strongest forever. In fact he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:08.880
wants to be surpassed. However, the major flaw&nbsp;
in Gojou’s thinking is that he can't help but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.080
resemble the system he was born and raised&nbsp;
in. NO matter how hard he tries to struggle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.000
he’s still a part of the system&nbsp;
he’s desperately trying to reform.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:24.080
And so the real struggle Gojo faces is that&nbsp;
despite his self-centeredness and his god complex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:28.880
deep down this man has a quite big heart&nbsp;
and sense of morality, that in the end makes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:34.000
him vulnerable to losses. Hanami and Jogo got&nbsp;
away because he prioritized Yuji's safety over&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:34.689
catching them and in general prioritizing Yuji's&nbsp;
education over winning which was why he was there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:34.689 --> 00:09:38.400
in the first place. Mahito was able to steal the&nbsp;
cursed objects from the school because he worried&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:43.520
and prioritized the lives of his students because&nbsp;
he determined the true loss would be their deaths.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:53.040
And so, based on his emotional&nbsp;
and compassionate side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.040 --> 00:09:59.920
the reason Gojo feels so incredibly lonely and&nbsp;
isolated is ironically enough his own strength&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:59.920 --> 00:10:05.120
and power. And this is represented by&nbsp;
the key symbol of Gojou’s character:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.760 --> 00:10:11.760
his eyes. The reason he wears sunglasses like&nbsp;
a blind man, and then a literal blindfold later&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.760 --> 00:10:19.120
on is due to the fact that he is always staring&nbsp;
into the infinity. He always sees everything.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:27.680
He’s literally so good at seeng through&nbsp;
people, at reading them, that they don’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:32.080
look like individual people to him. Every single&nbsp;
person on earth has a rich internal world filled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:40.960
with their own thoughts, emotions and biases. But&nbsp;
Gojou doesn’t perceive that. He only sees matter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:46.240
cursed energy, speed and so on and so forth.&nbsp;
Gojou has always distanced himself both from his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.240 --> 00:10:49.920
own feelings and the feelings of others. It’s&nbsp;
understandable considering the divide between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:54.000
Gojou and other people in the first place.&nbsp;
As a result, it’s really hard for him to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:55.746
other people as real people. To him they appear&nbsp;
like mere characters all reading off of a script.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.746 --> 00:10:55.840
As a result Gojo has always been distanced form&nbsp;
his own feelings and the feeling s of others.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.600
This distance shines through&nbsp;
in various ways. Notice it’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:02.080
always Gojo making the pop cultural references.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:16.720
He was the one who taught Itadori to handle his&nbsp;
emotions and cursed energy by literally making him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.720 --> 00:11:21.360
sit down and watch movie after movie. And while I&nbsp;
strongly belief that stories are done of the mots&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:28.000
powerful tools we as humans possess, having&nbsp;
feelings about fictional characters is nonetheless&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:34.784
not quite the same as having feelings for&nbsp;
a real person. Because instead of feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.784 --> 00:11:38.800
with people you are the silent observer on the&nbsp;
sideline. Granted the ability to see everything,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:44.720
life became more of a movie than reality, with&nbsp;
Gojo being the only one in the theater. Or,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:51.920
as the master himself would phrase it: "When&nbsp;
granted everything, you can't do anything ..."

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:58.480
Thus Gojo literally has to blind himself in order&nbsp;
to perceive other humans as actual people. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.480 --> 00:12:04.400
I think it's fair to call that quite tragic.&nbsp;
However, it also shows us once again that Gojo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:05.440 --> 00:12:12.160
cares. He cares that he can't see people. He cares&nbsp;
that he feels alone. And he cares that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:18.640
suffer under the current system. And yet he's&nbsp;
the strongest. Thus, Gojou is stripped down to&nbsp;&nbsp;

